  "evidencia": "Page: Cozy Tapes Vol. 2: Too Cozy. Sentence: 2: Too Cozy is the second studio album by American hip hop collective ASAP Mob.\nPage: Cozy Tapes Vol. 2: Too Cozy. Sentence: The album features guest appearances from Big Sean, Playboi Carti, Pro Era, Quavo, Lil Uzi Vert, Lil Yachty, Chief Keef, Gucci Mane, Schoolboy Q, Frank Ocean, Jaden Smith, Smooky Margielaa and Flatbush Zombies.\nPage: Frank Ocean. Sentence: Christopher Francis \"Frank\" Ocean (born Christopher Edwin Breaux; October 28, 1987) is an American singer and songwriter.\nPage: Frank Ocean. Sentence: Known for his idiosyncratic musical style, Ocean first embarked on a career as a ghostwriter, and in 2010 he became a member of hip hop collective Odd Future.\nPage: Swim Good. Sentence: \"Swim Good\" is a song by American singer Frank Ocean, released as the second single from his mixtape \"Nostalgia, Ultra\" (2011).",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Cozy Tapes Vol. 2: Too Cozy. Sentence: 2: Too Cozy is the second studio album by American hip hop collective ASAP Mob.\nPage: Cozy Tapes Vol. 2: Too Cozy. Sentence: The album features guest appearances from Big Sean, Playboi Carti, Pro Era, Quavo, Lil Uzi Vert, Lil Yachty, Chief Keef, Gucci Mane, Schoolboy Q, Frank Ocean, Jaden Smith, Smooky Margielaa and Flatbush Zombies.\nPage: Frank Ocean. Sentence: Christopher Francis \"Frank\" Ocean (born Christopher Edwin Breaux; October 28, 1987) is an American singer and songwriter.\nPage: Frank Ocean. Sentence: Known for his idiosyncratic musical style, Ocean first embarked on a career as a ghostwriter, and in 2010 he became a member of hip hop collective Odd Future.\nPage: Swim Good. Sentence: \"Swim Good\" is a song by American singer Frank Ocean, released as the second single from his mixtape \"Nostalgia, Ultra\" (2011).",
