        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Cozy Tapes Vol. 2: Too Cozy, Swim Good, Nostalgia, Ultra\n- People: Frank Ocean\n- Organizations: ASAP Mob, Odd Future\n- Topics: guest appearances, music career\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Ocean was born Christopher Edwin Breaux on October 28, 1987, and he is an American singer and songwriter.\n- In 2010, Frank Ocean became a member of the hip hop collective Odd Future after first starting his career as a ghostwriter.\n- \"Swim Good\" is a song by Frank Ocean that was released as the second single from his 2011 mixtape \"Nostalgia, Ultra\".\n- Cozy Tapes Vol. 2: Too Cozy is the second studio album by the American hip hop collective ASAP Mob.\n- Cozy Tapes Vol. 2: Too Cozy features guest appearances from Big Sean, Playboi Carti, Pro Era, Quavo, Lil Uzi Vert, Lil Yachty, Chief Keef, Gucci Mane, Schoolboy Q, Frank Ocean, Jaden Smith, Smooky Margielaa, and Flatbush Zombies.",
